WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.960
Australia just announced the world's first law forcing top ai companies to prove their models are safe before release. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 225. After that, a deep dive on how those safety checks actually work, Google putting its Chatbot in your car, and airlines drawing a hard line on booking tickets. Prime Minister Anthony Albanese's government, the Dakota Reports, is putting mandatory safety rules on advanced artificial intelligence, or ai.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.720
companies that operate in Australia. The rules sit under a plan the government

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.420
calls AI in Australia's interests, and they aim at the systems with the highest

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.100
risk. Those systems are called frontier models, which just means the biggest

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:48.040
most capable ones that can handle hard tasks across many different areas. Think of

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.980
the difference between a cheap handheld game and a top-tier console that runs

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:57.080
every kind of software you throw at it. The law is watching the consoles. Picture a

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:01.020
brand-new car that is not allowed on the road until it survives a crash test.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.540
The idea is to catch trouble early instead of waiting for a wreck.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:10.340
A new oversight body will work with the Australian AI Safety Institute, which is the team whose

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:14.840
job is watching these systems to enforce the rules and hand out steep penalties.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.180
Companies that build those frontier models will have to let outsiders inspect them, keep

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:25.360
running safety checks after launch, publish the playbook they use to stay safe, and tell

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.240
the government right away if something breaks.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.720
That last part is partly about AI agents, which are systems that do not just chat.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:37.520
They try to take actions on their own, and the government wants early warning if one of

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:42.360
those agents goes off the rails, like a robot vacuum that suddenly starts eating the cat

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:42.720
food.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:49.020
Albanese, Deputy Prime Minister Richard Morales, and Ministers Tony Burke and Tim Ayers said

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.240
Australia is putting those domestic guardrails in place before it walks into international

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:53.920
talks.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.220
Guardrails here are like the bumpers at a bowling alley.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.940
They are meant to keep a powerful throw from flying into the next lane.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:06.440
The stated goal is to protect people and national interests, while building the kind of trust

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:11.140
and stable rules that attract investment and let AI help the economy in healthcare.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.520
For you, that could mean the tools you use for school or creative projects get safer over

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:20.880
time, because companies will have to show their work instead of just promising they did.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:26.380
It also means AI is sliding from fun experiment toward something society's treat like other

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:30.640
high-risk tech, which can shape the jobs and tools waiting when you finish school.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.360
Here is a tiny version you can run today.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.580
Open the chat GPT website or the Gemini app, and type a homework-style word problem that

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.560
hides a trick, like using the wrong unit on purpose.

00:02:43.661 --> 00:02:47.261
Watch whether it catches the trap or cheerfully answers the wrong question.

00:02:47.261 --> 00:02:52.101
That little check is a homemade cousin of the much bigger tests this law wants done

00:02:52.101 --> 00:02:52.621
in public.

00:02:53.081 --> 00:02:56.621
A new phone usually gets a once over before it becomes your whole day.

00:02:57.241 --> 00:03:01.401
You open the camera, tap a few apps, and make sure nothing is obviously broken.

00:03:02.061 --> 00:03:07.341
Giant AI models now face a much bigger version of that same shakedown, and this is the part

00:03:07.341 --> 00:03:08.161
that clicked for me.

00:03:08.741 --> 00:03:13.581
Independent testers get the full model, not a shiny demo, the way a substitute teacher

00:03:13.581 --> 00:03:16.221
grades your test instead of letting you mark your own paper.

00:03:16.221 --> 00:03:21.761
They then run hundreds of trials on purpose, like pop quizzes designed to trip you up.

00:03:22.281 --> 00:03:25.561
One batch checks whether the model can be tricked into harmful advice.

00:03:26.141 --> 00:03:28.501
Another checks whether it leaks private information.

00:03:29.101 --> 00:03:32.201
Another checks whether it stays reliable when the request is weird.

00:03:32.781 --> 00:03:36.041
The way a calculator should still be right if you type the problem backwards.

00:03:36.641 --> 00:03:41.381
Those trials happen around launch, and they keep going afterward, because a system that

00:03:41.381 --> 00:03:43.841
looks fine on day one can still drift later.

00:03:43.841 --> 00:03:46.941
If problems show up, the builder has to fix them.

00:03:47.341 --> 00:03:51.721
The point is to turn safety from a company claim into something outsiders can actually

00:03:51.721 --> 00:03:56.361
verify, especially for the most powerful models that could affect many people at once.

00:03:57.041 --> 00:04:01.861
Once you see it as a giant, ongoing phone check run by people who do not work for the company,

00:04:02.381 --> 00:04:04.921
the whole audit idea feels a lot less mysterious.

00:04:06.053 --> 00:04:11.453
Google and gadget reports has dropped its Gemini chatbots straight into Apple CarPlay, so

00:04:11.453 --> 00:04:15.033
So you can talk to it on the car screen the same way you already do on your phone.

00:04:15.513 --> 00:04:20.973
A chatbot is just a program you can verse with in ordinary language and Gemini is Google's.

00:04:21.373 --> 00:04:24.853
CarPlay is the system that puts your iPhone's apps onto the dashboard.

00:04:25.413 --> 00:04:30.053
While you drive, you can ask for directions, check the weather, or get a quick answer without

00:04:30.053 --> 00:04:31.113
hopping between apps.

00:04:31.673 --> 00:04:36.413
It builds on the version already living inside Google Maps, so the same helpful voice shows

00:04:36.413 --> 00:04:38.473
up in more places you already use.

00:04:38.473 --> 00:04:41.933
Anyone with an iPhone and CarPlay can try it right now.

00:04:42.493 --> 00:04:48.073
Open the CarPlay screen, tap the Google app icon if you see it, or ask Siri to open Gemini

00:04:48.073 --> 00:04:51.253
then say, hey Google, what's the traffic like ahead?

00:04:51.873 --> 00:04:55.773
Make the question as natural as you would with a friend in the passenger seat who happens

00:04:55.773 --> 00:04:57.053
to know a lot of facts.

00:04:57.553 --> 00:05:02.393
Because the system already understands context from your phone, you can ask a follow-up without

00:05:02.393 --> 00:05:06.633
repeating yourself, the way a group chat remembers what you said two messages ago.

00:05:06.633 --> 00:05:11.340
Booking a plane ticket will stay a human job on United Airlines website.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.960
The Verge reports the airline will not let personal AI assistance buy tickets there, citing

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.080
privacy rules and government regulations.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:24.520
United wants a person in charge when payment and personal information are involved, and

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:29.520
it says it has not yet seen many people try to use AI agents to book, which matches what

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.280
businesses like DoorDash have noticed.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:37.788
2 million dollars is heading into research on how AI affects children, open AI said, to

00:05:37.788 --> 00:05:39.628
measure both the risks and the benefits.

00:05:40.168 --> 00:05:45.208
The aim is shared tools that parents, schools, and developers can use, a bit like a school

00:05:45.208 --> 00:05:49.908
funding a study on whether phones help or hurt homework, so everyone can read the same

00:05:49.908 --> 00:05:50.468
scorecard.

